<h1>Illinois Senate, 14th District</h1>
<p>Only some Senate seats are up this year.</p>
<p>On the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026.</p>
<h2>On the ballot</h2>
<ul>
<li><a href="/directdemocracy/app/election-candidate/2026-general--il-senate-14--emil-jones-iii">Emil Jones, III</a> (Democratic, Incumbent): His official site lists bringing more jobs to the 14th District, a responsible solution to the state budget, and ending business as usual in Springfield as his top priorities, with current legislative work on education…</li>
<li><a href="/directdemocracy/app/election-candidate/2026-general--il-senate-14--brian-skala">Brian Skala</a> (Republican): His campaign site lists lower taxes, lower utility bills, and safer communities as its key issues, along with job creation and keeping families in Illinois.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Write-in candidates</h2>
<p>These names are not printed on the ballot. To vote for one, write the name in the blank write-in space for that office and fill in the oval (on a touchscreen, follow the write-in steps on screen). Votes count only for write-ins who filed a declaration. The Chicago Board of Elections does not post those names, so this list comes from the Cook County Clerk&#39;s list and campaign announcements; election judges at your polling place have the official one.</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="/directdemocracy/app/election-candidate/2026-general--il-senate-14--paris-walker-thomas">Paris Walker Thomas</a> (Democratic, Write-in): Declared write-in candidate; the name is not printed on the ballot. No 2026 platform or campaign website found. In a 2024 candidate survey she named mental health, the rights of seniors, and domestic violence prevention…</li>
</ul>
